  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 10pt;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">Instructions for Homeowner</h3>
      <p>Homeowner's identification number. For your protection, this form may show only the last four digits of your social security number (SSN) or individual taxpayer identification number (ITIN). However, the IRS and other authorized agencies may require the full number, where applicable, to state and/or local governments.</p>
      <p><strong>Form 1098-MA.</strong> The information on this statement is submitted to the IRS by State Housing Finance Agencies (HFA) or the Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) to report mortgage assistance payments made by either HUD under the Emergency Homeowner Assistance Program (EHAP) or a State HFA under the Housing Finance Agency Innovations Program (HFA-I) or the Emergency Homeowner Assistance Program (EHAP) or a State HFA under the Housing Finance Agency Innovations Program (HFA-I). The payments made by you (homeowner mortgage payments) under this program are reported on this statement.</p>
      <p><strong>Safe-harbor deduction computation.</strong> You may use a safe-harbor method to compute your deduction for mortgage interest, premiums, and all of the related property taxes on your loan. If you use the safe-harbor method, you must use the same method for all of your mortgage interest on your loan, all of the mortgage insurance premiums, and all of the related property taxes paid on your loan. If you participated in an HFA Hardest Hit Fund program in which program payments could be used to pay mortgage interest or property taxes, you may use the safe-harbor method.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <p>deduct an amount equal to the sum of all payments you actually made during the year to your mortgage servicer, the State HFA, or HUD. However, the amount you may deduct cannot exceed the sum of all payments reported on this statement, in box 1 (Total State HFA/HUD and homeowner mortgage payments/borrower), and any real estate taxes and mortgage insurance premiums paid on your loan. If you are not using the safe-harbor method to compute your deduction for mortgage interest, mortgage insurance premiums, and real property taxes on your loan, you must use the amounts reported on this statement.</p>
      <p><strong>Account Number (optional).</strong> May show an account number the filer has assigned to distinguish your account.</p>
      <p><strong>Box 1.</strong> Shows the total amount of State HFA/HUD mortgage assistance payments and homeowner mortgage payments.</p>
      <p><strong>Box 2.</strong> Shows the amount of State HFA/HUD mortgage assistance payments.</p>
      <p><strong>Box 3.</strong> Shows the amount of homeowner mortgage payments you made during the year.</p>
      <p>For more information about developments related to Form 1098-MA and its instructions, such as changes in tax law, go to www.irs.gov/form1098ma.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 10pt;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">General instructions for Filer</h3>
      <p>General instructions are provided in the 2013 General Instructions for Certain Information Returns. This form is used to provide information to the IRS about mortgage assistance payments made by the homeowners receiving mortgage assistance payments made by the homeowners receiving mortgage assistance payments made by either HUD under the Emergency Homeowner Assistance Program (EHAP) or a State HFA under the Housing Finance Agency Innovations Program (HFA-I) or the Emergency Homeowner Assistance Program (EHAP) or a State HFA under the Housing Finance Agency Innovations Program (HFA-I).</p>
      <p><strong>File with IRS.</strong> File Copy A or a paper single statement in lieu of Copy A with the IRS at the following address:</p>
      <p>Internal Revenue Service Center</p>
      <p>Stop 6728A/USC</p>
      <p>Austin, TX 78701</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <p>If you file the paper single statement, it must contain each homeowner's name and federal identification number, and corresponding reportable amounts in boxes 1, 2, and 3 for each homeowner.</p>
      <p>Due dates. Furnish Copy B of this form or the statement to the recipient by January 31. File Copy A of this form or the statement with the IRS by January 31. If you are filing a paper return, you may request an extension of time for filing Copy A or the paper single statement in lieu of Copy A by filing Form 8809, Application for Extension of Time to File Information Returns, available on IRS.gov.</p>
      <p><strong>CAUTION</strong></p>
      <p>Form 1098-MA may not be filed electronically with the IRS. Form 1098-MA is not scanned during processing at the IRS. If you have questions about filing, call 1-800-829-1040.</p>
      <p><strong>Need help?</strong> If you have questions about reporting on Form 1098-MA, contact the IRS at 1-800-829-1040. For questions about filing or speech disability with access to TTY/TDD equipment call 304-579-4827 (not toll free).</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>